IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wc-rules`

-- War Crimes Act 1945 (Cth) — the encoder's tests.

§ `Tests`

`violent` MEANS `murder, manslaughter, grievous bodily harm, wounding, rape, indecent assault or abduction, or a variant or complicity in one`
`camp` MEANS `deporting or interning a person in a death camp, slave labour camp or like place, or complicity in it`

GIVEN k IS A `Act kind`, off IS A BOOLEAN, conn IS A `Connection`, eur IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A DATE, kill IS A BOOLEAN, cit IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `War crime case`
`an act` k `an offence then` off `connected` conn `in Europe` eur `on` d `killing` kill `citizen` cit MEANS
    `War crime case` OF k, off, conn, eur, d, kill, cit, FALSE, FALSE

`occupation` MEANS `in the course of an occupation`

#ASSERT `it is a war crime` (`an act` `violent` `an offence then` TRUE `connected` `occupation` `in Europe` TRUE `on` (Date 1 6 1942) `killing` TRUE `citizen` TRUE)
#ASSERT `I may be charged` (`an act` `violent` `an offence then` TRUE `connected` `occupation` `in Europe` TRUE `on` (Date 1 6 1942) `killing` TRUE `citizen` TRUE)
#ASSERT (`the war crime position for` (`an act` `violent` `an offence then` TRUE `connected` `occupation` `in Europe` TRUE `on` (Date 1 6 1942) `killing` TRUE `citizen` TRUE))'s `I may be imprisoned for life`
#ASSERT `the other maximum for` (`an act` `violent` `an offence then` TRUE `connected` `occupation` `in Europe` TRUE `on` (Date 1 6 1942) `killing` FALSE `citizen` TRUE) EQUALS 25
-- s 11
#ASSERT NOT (`I may be charged` (`an act` `violent` `an offence then` TRUE `connected` `occupation` `in Europe` TRUE `on` (Date 1 6 1942) `killing` TRUE `citizen` FALSE))
-- the period edges
#ASSERT `it is a war crime` (`an act` `violent` `an offence then` TRUE `connected` `occupation` `in Europe` TRUE `on` (Date 1 9 1939) `killing` TRUE `citizen` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`it is a war crime` (`an act` `violent` `an offence then` TRUE `connected` `occupation` `in Europe` TRUE `on` (Date 31 8 1939) `killing` TRUE `citizen` TRUE))
#ASSERT `it is a war crime` (`an act` `violent` `an offence then` TRUE `connected` `occupation` `in Europe` TRUE `on` (Date 8 5 1945) `killing` TRUE `citizen` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`it is a war crime` (`an act` `violent` `an offence then` TRUE `connected` `occupation` `in Europe` TRUE `on` (Date 9 5 1945) `killing` TRUE `citizen` TRUE))
-- outside Europe; incidental connection
#ASSERT NOT (`it is a war crime` (`an act` `violent` `an offence then` TRUE `connected` `occupation` `in Europe` FALSE `on` (Date 1 6 1942) `killing` TRUE `citizen` TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`it is a war crime` (`an act` `violent` `an offence then` TRUE `connected` `only incidental or remote` `in Europe` TRUE `on` (Date 1 6 1942) `killing` TRUE `citizen` TRUE))
-- s 6(4), (6): deportation to a camp, whatever the local law
#ASSERT `it is a serious crime` (`an act` `camp` `an offence then` FALSE `connected` `in persecution or genocide, in a country at war or occupied` `in Europe` TRUE `on` (Date 1 6 1942) `killing` FALSE `citizen` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`it is a serious crime` (`an act` `violent` `an offence then` FALSE `connected` `occupation` `in Europe` TRUE `on` (Date 1 6 1942) `killing` FALSE `citizen` TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`it is a serious crime` (`an act` `another act` `an offence then` TRUE `connected` `occupation` `in Europe` TRUE `on` (Date 1 6 1942) `killing` FALSE `citizen` TRUE))
-- s 17
#ASSERT `the laws of war are a defence` (`War crime case` OF `violent`, TRUE, `in the course of hostilities in a war`, TRUE, Date 1 6 1942, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the laws of war are a defence` (`War crime case` OF `violent`, TRUE, `in the course of hostilities in a war`, TRUE, Date 1 6 1942, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE))
